{{!--
    One line on the slate. Used twice — buying and selling — which differ only in
    which map the quantity is written to and which action removes it, so both ride
    on the line itself rather than being two copies of this markup.

    A single row, unlike a shelf row: icon, name, quantity, price. The name takes
    whatever width is left and ellipsises, because a slate is a narrow column and
    "Cordial of Holiday Insight" will not fit in it whatever else is done.
--}}
<div class="merchant-shop-cart-line" data-item-id="{{id}}">
    <img src="{{img}}" alt="">
    <span class="merchant-shop-cart-name" data-tooltip="{{name}}">{{name}}</span>
    <span class="merchant-shop-cart-qty merchant-shop-qty-editable"
          data-edit-line="{{id}}" data-line-side="{{side}}"
          data-tooltip="Double-click to change; 0 removes it">&times;<strong>{{quantity}}</strong></span>
    <span class="merchant-shop-cart-total">{{totalLabel}}</span>
    {{!-- Last, at the far edge: removing is the one destructive thing on the line,
          so it sits apart from the numbers rather than beside one of them. --}}
    <button type="button" class="merchant-shop-cart-remove" data-action="{{removeAction}}"
            data-item-id="{{id}}" data-tooltip="Take it off the slate">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
    </button>
</div>
